<title>USA: PG&amp;E Corp Q4 shr drops to $0.34 vs $0.48.</title>
<headline>PG&amp;E Corp Q4 shr drops to $0.34 vs $0.48.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.34		    $0.48</p>
<p> Net			149,030		  227,085</p>
<p> Revs		   2,700,686		2,227,224</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 408,982		  416,655</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.75		    $2.99</p>
<p> Net			755,209		1,338,885</p>
<p> Revs		   9,609,972		9,621,765</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 412,542		  423,692</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Earnings for the latest twelve-months include charges of $182 million ($0.26 per share) for contingencies related to gas transportation commitments and an increase in litigation costs of $67 million ($0.10 per share).</p>
<p>Earnings per share decreased for the latest three- and twelve-month periods due primarily to $59 million ($0.09 per share) of write downs of PG&amp;E's nonregulated investments.</p>
</text>
